44
00:51:54.730 --> 00:51:55.730
How beautiful is that?

45
00:51:56.730 --> 00:52:03.730
Actually, sometimes, when you look at it, I know that Mathijs has certainly given something to me, once for Father's Day or something like that.

46
00:52:04.730 --> 00:52:08.730
And then you think, there has been thought put into this.

47
00:52:09.730 --> 00:52:11.730
Something has been given from a good heart.

48
00:52:12.730 --> 00:52:17.730
And you give it a place of honor in my office.

49
00:52:18.730 --> 00:52:20.730
And this is how we should look at giving.

50
00:52:22.730 --> 00:52:25.730
Actually, God has everything.

51
00:52:26.730 --> 00:52:32.730
He has everything, so what we give, He really does not need.

52
00:52:33.730 --> 00:52:37.730
But He wants us to think about it and to apply that principle.

53
00:52:38.730 --> 00:52:39.730
And that is true giving.

54
00:52:41.730 --> 00:52:49.730
Heavenly Father, I want to pray that you are the one who will bless what we bring back.

55
00:52:50.730 --> 00:52:57.730
I truly want to pray, Lord God, that the principle of giving and thinking about what we are going to give.

56
00:52:58.730 --> 00:53:05.730
And the realization that what we give, we have received from you, will truly penetrate our hearts.

57
00:53:06.730 --> 00:53:08.730
We owe everything to you.

58
00:53:09.730 --> 00:53:12.730
Our life, what you have given us.

59
00:53:13.730 --> 00:53:18.730
Lord God, live this principle in our hearts and let it become clear.

60
00:53:19.730 --> 00:53:24.730
And as we apply it, as your Word says, it is not a command.

61
00:53:25.730 --> 00:53:31.730
Lord God, it is a call to show how real our love for you is.

62
00:53:32.730 --> 00:53:34.730
I pray this, Lord God, in the name of Jesus.

63
00:53:35.730 --> 00:53:37.730
And that you will bless what is being brought in.

64
00:53:38.730 --> 00:53:40.730
In your wonderful name. Amen.

