171
01:01:29.730 --> 01:01:33.730
Because you know that you are doing something wrong and every time you do it again.

172
01:01:35.730 --> 01:01:38.730
And every time you feel guilty again.

173
01:01:38.730 --> 01:01:41.730
And every time you say, Lord forgive me.

174
01:01:41.730 --> 01:01:46.730
I must be very honest, there was a very long period in my life that I prayed for that almost daily.

175
01:01:49.730 --> 01:01:56.730
And then I felt that God at some point said to me, Tim I want you to grow up because I want you to take more authority

176
01:01:56.730 --> 01:02:02.730
than having to stand at the starting blocks every day praying for forgiveness again.

177
01:02:02.730 --> 01:02:07.730
I have called you as a son of mine to take more authority over life

178
01:02:07.730 --> 01:02:13.730
than having to say every time, Lord I am so sorry and I won't do it again tomorrow.

179
01:02:13.730 --> 01:02:18.730
And the next day you do it again and oh Lord I am so sorry, I shouldn't have done that.

180
01:02:18.730 --> 01:02:23.730
I shouldn't have said that, I shouldn't have watched that, I shouldn't have acted that way.

181
01:02:23.730 --> 01:02:25.730
I am so sorry, I am so sorry.

182
01:02:25.730 --> 01:02:29.730
The prayer of forgiveness is really good, we will come back to that shortly.

183
01:02:29.730 --> 01:02:32.730
Only God wants us to rise to a higher level.

184
01:02:33.730 --> 01:02:42.730
So here is a question and I mean it, so don't just listen to this question but bring it to yourself in reflection.

185
01:02:42.730 --> 01:02:45.730
What prayers do you actually pray?

186
01:02:45.730 --> 01:02:48.730
What do you pray for daily?

187
01:02:50.730 --> 01:02:56.730
And if you don't pray at all, go pray.

188
01:02:57.730 --> 01:02:58.730
Pray.

189
01:03:00.730 --> 01:03:03.730
Pray to God.

190
01:03:05.730 --> 01:03:06.730
Daily.

191
01:03:09.730 --> 01:03:19.730
And it is actually bizarre that I feel this way this past week, to present this in a church.

192
01:03:19.730 --> 01:03:27.730
It is actually bizarre to realize that the children of God pray too little.

193
01:03:29.730 --> 01:03:32.730
It is not a slap in the face to anyone.

194
01:03:32.730 --> 01:03:39.730
I am trying to instill a conviction in us, I am trying to motivate us in the name of Jesus.

195
01:03:39.730 --> 01:03:48.730
That we are a holy nation and that we are called by God himself to speak in His authority.

196
01:03:50.730 --> 01:03:57.730
The very first provision that God made when He created heaven and earth,

197
01:03:57.730 --> 01:04:08.730
was not so much the trees and the beautiful animals and the grass and the wonderful everything that God has made.

198
01:04:08.730 --> 01:04:12.730
And you may eat anything and you may enjoy everything.

199
01:04:12.730 --> 01:04:19.730
That provision was not the primary provision of what God could give at the beginning of creation.

200
01:04:20.730 --> 01:04:28.730
The most beautiful thing that God could give was Himself.

201
01:04:28.730 --> 01:04:41.730
Imagine a time when you can walk through a forest and God can walk with you in the evening coolness.

202
01:04:41.730 --> 01:04:48.730
The Father, the almighty one, Creator of heaven and earth.

203
01:04:49.730 --> 01:04:53.730
He who breathes out planets.

204
01:04:53.730 --> 01:04:59.730
He who holds everything, the entire universe, in His hands.

205
01:04:59.730 --> 01:05:06.730
In person, He walks with Adam through the garden.

206
01:05:06.730 --> 01:05:10.730
How amazing must that be?

207
01:05:11.730 --> 01:05:18.730
So the first provision of God was Himself from heaven.

208
01:05:18.730 --> 01:05:22.730
And He created humanity around that.

209
01:05:22.730 --> 01:05:28.730
He is the most beautiful, and to share His beauty,

210
01:05:28.730 --> 01:05:34.730
He creates humanity around Him so that humanity can walk with Him.

211
01:05:35.730 --> 01:05:41.730
We are added to Him to enjoy Him. Amen?

212
01:05:43.730 --> 01:05:45.730
So that is the first.

213
01:05:46.730 --> 01:05:51.730
Then I see a moment arise where, we know the story.

214
01:05:51.730 --> 01:05:58.730
Humanity loses the intimate contact with God. What a horror.

215
01:05:59.730 --> 01:06:09.730
And ultimately, after years, years, years, this is the story on which this year's theme is based.

216
01:06:09.730 --> 01:06:18.730
So you have the story that God calls Abraham to give his son to God.

217
01:06:18.730 --> 01:06:24.730
And Abraham takes his son Isaac up a mountain.

218
01:06:24.730 --> 01:06:32.730
